 4. 📉 Charted: CEO mood sours 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: The Conference Board and The Business Council. Chart: Axios/Emily Peck CEO confidence in the U.S. economy sank into negative territory earlier this month, Axios' Emily Peck writes from a Conference Board survey out this morning. 

 The CEO Confidence Index — a survey of 131 Fortune 500 CEOs — fell to 46, down from 52 just three months ago. Any number below 50 signals negative sentiment. ⚠️ Threat level: 41% of CEOs expected economic conditions to worsen — up from 19% in the previous quarter.

 Executives' concerns over cybersecurity, AI and geopolitics rose significantly from three months ago. Keep reading . 

 
 
